<%- include('partials/generator') %>

<div class="wrap prose">
  <h2 id="requirements">Factuurvereisten: what the Belastingdienst requires</h2>
  <p>A Dutch VAT invoice must show these details. The numbers refer to the example above.</p>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Required field (Dutch)</th><th>In English</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td class="strong">Volledige naam van u en uw afnemer</td><td>Full legal name of you and your client (a trade name is fine if it is registered at KVK with its address)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td class="strong">Volledig adres van u en uw afnemer</td><td>Full address of both; a PO box alone is not enough</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td class="strong">Uw btw-identificatienummer</td><td>Your VAT ID, the number starting with NL</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td class="strong">Uw KVK-nummer (als u bij de KVK bent ingeschreven)</td><td>Your Chamber of Commerce number, if registered</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5</td><td class="strong">Factuurdatum</td><td>Date the invoice is issued</td></tr>
      <tr><td>6</td><td class="strong">Factuurnummer</td><td>Unique, sequential number; one or more series allowed, each number used once</td></tr>
      <tr><td>7</td><td class="strong">Omschrijving en hoeveelheid / omvang</td><td>What goods or services you supplied, and how much</td></tr>
      <tr><td>8</td><td class="strong">Leverdatum</td><td>Date of supply, or the date of an advance payment</td></tr>
      <tr><td>9</td><td class="strong">Bedrag exclusief btw</td><td>Amount excluding VAT, per rate if you use several rates, with the unit price where relevant</td></tr>
      <tr><td>10</td><td class="strong">Btw-tarief</td><td>The VAT rate that applies</td></tr>
      <tr><td>11</td><td class="strong">Btw-bedrag</td><td>The VAT amount</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="source">Source: <a href="<%= BD.eisen %>" rel="noopener">Belastingdienst, factuureisen</a> (English: <a href="<%= BD.eisenEn %>" rel="noopener">invoice requirements</a>) and <a href="<%= BD.kvk %>" rel="noopener">KVK on the KVK number</a>. Checked <%= checked %>.</p>
  <p>Not legally required but expected: a due date (vervaldatum), your IBAN and the payment reference. Without an agreed term, Dutch law gives your client 30 days to pay; between businesses the maximum is generally 60 days (<a href="<%= BD.termijn %>" rel="noopener">Ondernemersplein</a>).</p>

  <h2>BTW rates in 2026</h2>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th class="num">Rate</th><th>Name</th><th>Applies to</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="num strong">21%</td><td>Algemeen tarief (standard)</td><td>Most goods and services: consulting, design, software, electronics, and since 1 January 2026 hotel and holiday accommodation</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="num strong">9%</td><td>Verlaagd tarief (reduced)</td><td>Goods and services on the reduced list, such as food, non-alcoholic drinks, books, medicines and some services</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="num strong">0%</td><td>Nultarief</td><td>Exports outside the EU and certain supplies to businesses in other EU countries</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="source">Sources: <a href="<%= BD.tarief %>" rel="noopener">Belastingdienst, btw-tarief</a>; <a href="<%= BD.logies %>" rel="noopener">btw op logies</a> (accommodation at 21% from 1 January 2026). Checked <%= checked %>.</p>
  <p>Some activities are <strong>vrijgesteld</strong> (exempt) rather than 0%, for example most medical care and education. Exempt services carry no BTW line at all.</p>

  <h3>BTW calculator</h3>
  <div class="calc">
    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="bAmt">Amount (EUR)</label><input type="number" id="bAmt" value="1000" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal"></div>
      <div><label for="bRate">BTW rate</label><select id="bRate"><option value="21">21%</option><option value="9">9%</option><option value="0">0%</option></select></div>
      <div><label for="bMode">The amount is</label><select id="bMode"><option value="add">excl. BTW</option><option value="remove">incl. BTW</option></select></div>
    </div>
    <div class="res" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="line"><span>Excl. BTW</span><span id="bEx"></span></div>
      <div class="line"><span id="bLbl">BTW 21%</span><span id="bBtw"></span></div>
      <div class="line total"><span>Incl. BTW</span><span id="bInc"></span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="formula">BTW = amount excl. BTW x 0.21 (or 0.09)<br>Amount excl. BTW = amount incl. BTW / 1.21 (or 1.09)<br><b>&euro; 1.850,00 x 0.21 = &euro; 388,50 BTW, total &euro; 2.238,50</b></div>

  <h2>KVK number, btw-id and omzetbelastingnummer</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>KVK-nummer</strong>: 8 digits, given when you register at the Chamber of Commerce (KVK). It must be on your invoices, quotes, letters, website and business emails. There is no way to generate a real one; use your own.</li>
    <li><strong>Btw-id</strong> (btw-identificatienummer): <code>NL</code> + 9 digits + <code>B</code> + 2 digits, for example <code>NL123456789B01</code>. This is the VAT number for your invoices and website.</li>
    <li><strong>Omzetbelastingnummer</strong> (ob-nummer): only for contact with the Belastingdienst. For a zzp'er it is a different number from the btw-id, so do not put it on invoices.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="source">Sources: <a href="<%= BD.kvk %>" rel="noopener">KVK</a>, <a href="<%= BD.btwid %>" rel="noopener">Belastingdienst, btw-id en omzetbelastingnummer</a>. Checked <%= checked %>.</p>

  <h2>Special cases</h2>
  <h3>Reverse charge: "btw verlegd"</h3>
  <p>When the VAT is shifted to your client (for example certain services to a business in another EU country), you charge no BTW. Write <strong>"btw verlegd"</strong> on the invoice together with <strong>the client's btw-id</strong>, and still show the amount per BTW rate. Your own btw-id must be on the invoice as well. In the generator, set the tax rate to 0, put the client's VAT number in the client tax ID field and the words "btw verlegd" in the notes. Source: <a href="<%= BD.verlegd %>" rel="noopener">Belastingdienst, verleggingsregeling</a>.</p>
  <h3>Small business scheme (KOR)</h3>
  <p>With turnover up to <strong>&euro; 20.000 per calendar year</strong> you can use the kleineondernemersregeling. You then charge no BTW and state on the invoice that you use the KOR, for example "Vrijgesteld van btw op grond van de kleineondernemersregeling". Leave the tax field empty in the generator. Sources: <a href="<%= BD.kor %>" rel="noopener">KOR</a>, <a href="<%= BD.korFactuur %>" rel="noopener">invoices under the KOR</a>.</p>
  <h3>Simplified invoice up to &euro; 100</h3>
  <p>For invoices of at most &euro; 100 including BTW, a simplified invoice is allowed: the date, your name and address, what you supplied, and the BTW (or the details to calculate it). It is not allowed for intra-EU supplies, distance sales and some reverse-charge cases. Source: <a href="<%= BD.vereenvoudigd %>" rel="noopener">vereenvoudigde factuur</a>.</p>
  <h3>Clients outside the Netherlands</h3>
  <p>Whether you charge Dutch BTW to a foreign client depends on what you supply, where the client is and whether the client is a business. The <a href="<%= BD.buitenland %>" rel="noopener">Belastingdienst guide to doing business abroad</a> walks through each case.</p>
  <h3>Keep your invoices</h3>
  <p>Keep copies of all invoices for <strong>7 years</strong>; records about real estate for 10 years (<a href="<%= BD.bewaren %>" rel="noopener">Belastingdienst</a>).</p>

  <h2>Dutch invoice terms in English</h2>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Dutch</th><th>English</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="strong">Factuur</td><td>Invoice</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Factuurnummer</td><td>Invoice number</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Factuurdatum</td><td>Invoice date</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Leverdatum</td><td>Date of supply</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Vervaldatum</td><td>Due date</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Omschrijving</td><td>Description</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Aantal / Prijs / Bedrag</td><td>Quantity / Unit price / Amount</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Subtotaal excl. btw</td><td>Subtotal excluding VAT</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Btw / Totaal incl. btw</td><td>VAT / Total including VAT</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Btw verlegd</td><td>VAT reverse-charged to the client</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Vrijgesteld van btw</td><td>Exempt from VAT</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Creditfactuur / creditnota</td><td>Credit note</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">Betalingstermijn</td><td>Payment term</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">O.v.v. (onder vermelding van)</td><td>Quoting (the reference)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

